<title>USA: Varian sees second-half 1997 improvement.</title>
<headline>Varian sees second-half 1997 improvement.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Varian Associates Inc on Thursday blamed its lower revenues for the first half of fiscal 1997 on a worldwide slowdown in semiconductor equipment demand and on the strong dollar, but said it expected some improvement in the second half.</p>
<p>The company said the slowdown in the demand for semiconductor manufacturing equipment seemed to have bottomed out.</p>
<p>Other factors mentioned as hurting first-quarter results were a brief strike at an Australian equipment factory and some shipment stretch-outs in the health-care sector.</p>
<p>These factors plus the strong dollar had a negative but largely temporary effect on sales, the company said.</p>
</text>
